   "id": "8326592",
   "item_level": "6",
   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 14710092,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 2062409,
    "poster_id": 363884,
    "post_rendered": "Given a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/520df6c71065c91174d0ed0d562ebd3c5980267f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\times n$\"  width=\"48\" height=\"9\" > grid rectangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/8324227f5261effd0fd48fdee7d3712e0b2e9d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" > and a closed path <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > that is not self intersecting from inner points of the grid, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > be the number of points on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > does not turn in them and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > be the number of squares that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > goes through two non-adjacent sides of them furthermore let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > be the number of squares with no side in <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8137e79456d93455c89a6a83affb2f9047bae4ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$A=B-C+m+n-1.$$\"  width=\"194\" height=\"14\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Given a $m\\times n$ grid rectangle with $m,n \\ge 4$ and a closed path $P$ that is not self intersecting from inner points of the grid, let $A$ be the number of points on $P$ such that $P$ does not turn in them and let $B$ be the number of squares that $P$ goes through two non-adjacent sides of them furthermore let $C$ be the number of squares with no side in $P$. Prove that $$A=B-C+m+n-1.$$",
    "username": "matinyousefi",
