   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 14710222,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 2062418,
    "poster_id": 363884,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > be an acute-angled triangle with circumcircle <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\"  width=\"11\" height=\"8\" >.</span> Prove that there exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\"  width=\"12\" height=\"12\" > such that for any point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b5b9f47b00a8855e214bba05bb8b07679f011ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX,BX,CX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" > intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\"  width=\"11\" height=\"8\" > in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/7/5a7c6b51961d859489bdf038ec21f2c17720c448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1,B_1,C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c5129ccd84a78293a5830cc0bc8d4cddf4b629f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2,B_2,C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" > be reflections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/7/5a7c6b51961d859489bdf038ec21f2c17720c448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1,B_1,C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" > in midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e6f986f83255f04596f3cee8797d46f3c40177a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC,AC,AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" > respectively then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e299f9b67f8e09f3f280bbd438e6df4dceb5d01e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2,B_2,C_2,J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" > lie on a circle.",
    "post_canonical": "Let $ABC$ be an acute-angled triangle with circumcircle $\\omega$. Prove that there exists a point $J$ such that for any point $X$ inside $ABC$ if $AX,BX,CX$ intersect $\\omega$ in $A_1,B_1,C_1$ and $A_2,B_2,C_2$ be reflections of $A_1,B_1,C_1$ in midpoints of $BC,AC,AB$ respectively then $A_2,B_2,C_2,J$ lie on a circle. ",
    "username": "matinyousefi",
