   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 14710659,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 2062448,
    "poster_id": 363884,
    "post_rendered": "Two concentric circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee1dd9170f4dc324ad1f2c57f1bb478677d2b1fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega, \\Omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" > with radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/f/a1f66a1478e949636079558d0bf44928fa3f77b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8,13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" > are given. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" > is a diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\"  width=\"12\" height=\"13\" > and the tangent from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\"  width=\"11\" height=\"8\" > touches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\"  width=\"11\" height=\"8\" > at <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" >.</span> What is the length of <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"13\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "Two concentric circles $\\omega, \\Omega$ with radii $8,13$ are given. $AB$ is a diameter of $\\Omega$ and the tangent from $B$ to $\\omega$ touches $\\omega$ at $D$. What is the length of $AD$.",
